From 16ade5f0b9de60cb26352a72febe9e963c4a593c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flashnext <flashnext@leger.run>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:05:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] flashnext: pin build-system torch to 2.11.0 for the
 gfx1151 substrate

The gfx1151 (Strix Halo) build substrate ships exactly one torch: the AMD
TheRock wheel torch 2.11.0+rocm7.15.0a20260719 for cp313. pyproject.toml
carried the CUDA build number (2.13.0) while requirements/build/rocm.txt
already pins torch==2.11.0, so the ROCm build path was already designed
around 2.11 -- only [build-system].requires disagreed.

Audited before changing: no PR-added code needs a torch >=2.12 API.
  - vllm/models/qwen4_exp/**, vllm/v1/spec_decode/qwen4_exp.py and
    vllm/transformers_utils/configs/qwen4_exp.py use only long-stable
    torch symbols (torch.float8_e4m3fn, torch.frombuffer, torch.cummax,
    torch.searchsorted, ...) plus vllm's own direct_register_custom_op.
  - the PR-added csrc (csrc/libtorch_stable/{gdn/fused_gdn_decode_kernel.cu,
    ops.h,torch_bindings.cpp}) only widens an existing signature by a
    std::string; every torch::stable:: / torch::headeronly:: symbol used
    anywhere in csrc/ resolves in torch 2.11.0's shipped headers.
  - vllm/env_override.py:525,563,728 still carries the explicit
    'torch >= 2.11 and < 2.12' backports, i.e. upstream at this commit
    still supports 2.11.

This literal is also what nix-strix-halo overlays/therock-vllm.nix:269
matches with --replace-fail '"torch == 2.11.0"'; a miss is a hard build
abort. Note requirements/build/cuda.txt:8 intentionally stays at 2.13.0.
---
 pyproject.toml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 0766645..34af18a 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -7,7 +7,10 @@ requires = [
     "setuptools>=77.0.3,<81.0.0",
     "setuptools-scm>=8.0",
     "setuptools-rust>=1.9.0",
-    "torch == 2.13.0",
+    # flashnext: pinned to the ROCm build torch (requirements/build/rocm.txt),
+    # not the CUDA 2.13.0 line, because the gfx1151 substrate only ships
+    # torch 2.11.0. vllm/env_override.py still carries the <2.12 backports.
+    "torch == 2.11.0",
     "wheel",
     "jinja2",
 ]
-- 
